# The launcher hashed the binary before exec (correct, and the point of the discipline) but
# also printed "repo HEAD = 4e6f85d", which ASSERTS a relationship it did not verify: that
# the binary was built from that commit. The `cargo build` immediately before this launch
# FAILED -- another lane was mid-edit on a new workspace member, holon-resource -- so the
# binary that ran is an earlier successful build, not one from 4e6f85d.
#
# The hash is still exactly right; it names the bytes that ran. It is the HEAD line that
# overreaches. Read the two together as "these bytes ran, while the repo was at 4e6f85d",
# never as "these bytes were built from 4e6f85d".
#
# What the binary actually is can be read off its own echoed parameters, which is the whole
# reason they are echoed: "target = 1e-10, bar = 1e-9" places it AFTER 179db95, so it is a
# post-bar-re-derivation build. That is the identification that holds.
#
